Cage: add wlr-foreign-toplevel-management (wlrctl toplevel focus/close).

Backport of upstream commit af0a3cf8 (cage-kiosk/cage, Dec 2025, in v0.3.0) to
Cage 0.2.0 / wlroots 0.18 as shipped by Debian 13. Differences from upstream:
- 0.2.0 names the handler handle_xdg_shell_surface_request_fullscreen.
- Every handle call is guarded: the handle exists only while the view is mapped,
  and 0.2.0 delivers request_fullscreen before map (foot --fullscreen).
- Title, app_id and class are set only when present (wlroots strdup()s them).
- A view raised through the protocol moves to the front of server->views, so
  closing a window (the on-screen keyboard) focuses the one raised last.
CouchLiteOS needs it so Guide/Home brings the launcher over a running app.
Applied with patch -p1 by config/live-build/hooks/live/0050-cage.hook.chroot.

